{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Hardware dequantization and SIMD-group matrix multiplication for 4-bit and 8-bit quantized weights on Apple Silicon GPU.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError"],"anchor":"Quantization--Metal-Execution","title":"Quantization & Metal Execution"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalshadersquantization"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Native Metal MSL Shaders for Quantized LLMs"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Large language models like Llama 3, Mistral, and DeepSeek require massive memory bandwidth. Weight-only quantization (such as GGUF Q4_0 and Q8_0) compresses 16-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit or 8-bit integer blocks with group scaling factors, reducing memory footprint by 50% to 75%."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implements native Metal Shading Language (MSL) SIMD kernels executing hardware dequantization and GEMV \/ GEMM transformations directly on Apple Silicon GPUs without intermediate CPU memory allocations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Architecture","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Architecture"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Packed Quantized Weights [Q4_0 \/ Q8_0]   Scale Factors [FP16]   Input Activations [FP32]","                 │                               │                        │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────┴────────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                   Metal Compute Command Encoder","                                         │","                 ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐","                 ▼                                               ▼","     MSL Kernel: gemv_q4_0                           MSL Kernel: gemv_q8_0","   - Unpack 4-bit nibbles (w - 8)                  - Load signed 8-bit integers","   - Multiply by group FP16 scale                  - Multiply by group FP16 scale","   - Accumulate with input vector                  - Accumulate with input vector","                 │                                               │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                            Output Activation Vector","                               (Unified Memory)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"SIMD-Group-Matrix-Multiplication","type":"heading","text":"SIMD-Group Matrix Multiplication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On Apple Silicon (M-series GPUs), threads within a 32-thread SIMD-group collaborate on 8x8 matrix tiles using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"metal_simdgroup_matrix"},{"text":". This eliminates thread divergence and ensures maximal utilization of the GPU arithmetic units:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"metal","code":["#include <metal_stdlib>","#include <metal_simdgroup_matrix>","","using namespace metal;","","kernel void gemm_simdgroup_q4_0(","    device const half* A               [[buffer(0)]],","    device const half* B               [[buffer(1)]],","    device half* C                     [[buffer(2)]],","    constant uint& M                   [[buffer(3)]],","    constant uint& N                   [[buffer(4)]],","    constant uint& K                   [[buffer(5)]],","    uint2 threadgroup_position_in_grid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],","    uint simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]",") {","    simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8> acc;","    acc = make_filled_simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8>(0.0h);","    \/\/ Accumulate across inner K dimension...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Swift-API-Integration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Swift API Integration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"QuantizedLinear"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes both MLX tensor inference and direct Metal kernel execution:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftLLM","","\/\/ 1. Create a quantized linear layer (e.g. 4096 in, 4096 out)","let linear = QuantizedLinear(","    inFeatures: 4096,","    outFeatures: 4096,","    scheme: .q4_0,","    weight: mlxWeights,","    scales: mlxScales",")","","\/\/ 2. Direct Metal shader execution without CPU round-trips","let outputs = try linear.forwardMetal(","    inVector: inputActivations,","    rawWeights: packedQ4Bytes,","    rawScales: fp16Scales",")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/TransformerDecoderArchitecture":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"High-throughput, on-device causal language model execution on Apple Silicon Unified Memory Architecture using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TransformerDecoder"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PagedKVCache"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GGUFParser"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SafeTensorsParser"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"ur